    takeaway:
      "The four profiles show that psychosocial resources do not translate into burnout outcomes in a simple linear way. A person-centered approach reveals distinct teacher segments with different resource configurations, burnout risks, and support needs.",
    insights: [
      {
        title: "Burnout is heterogeneous.",
        text: "Teachers with similar overall burnout scores may still show different patterns across emotional exhaustion, depersonalization, and personal accomplishment.",
      },
      {
        title: "Person-centered analysis can reveal hidden needs.",
        text: "Different burnout profiles may require different types of support rather than one-size-fits-all interventions.",
      },
      {
        title: "Statistical segmentation can support targeted strategy.",
        text: "By identifying distinct profiles, research findings can be translated into more precise support recommendations for schools, organizations, or service systems.",
      },
